menu "Lichen display"
    config LICHEN_DISPLAY_DIRECT_FLUSH
        bool "Rotate LVGL strips straight into the panel frame buffer"
        default y
        help
            Lichen's own flush callback turns each rendered 720x80 strip by 90 degrees directly into the DSI
            panel's frame buffer, instead of esp_lvgl_port rotating it into a second PSRAM buffer and the DPI
            driver copying that into the frame buffer with DMA2D (#95). Saves two PSRAM passes per strip and
            the port's 112 KB rotation buffer. Tear-free since #467: strips go into the second frame buffer,
            which is swapped in at the end of the frame. Off = the port's path, untouched (one buffer shown).
            What turns the strip is chosen at runtime (#468, #475): the PPA in the background at every boot, in both
            builds, with a fallback to the CPU; in a developer build the registry key disp.engine switches to cpu.
endmenu
